      "final_text_tail": "dition.\n\nLet me reconsider the problem. The issue is:\n- For `Decimal('1e-200')` with `decimal_pos=2`: The number is `1e-200`. With 2 decimal places, this rounds to `0.00`. The fix should return `0.00`.\n- For `Decimal('1e-200')` with `decimal_pos=200`: The number is `1e-200`. With 200 decimal places, this should be `0.000...001` (199 zeros, then 1). But the current fix returns `1.00e-200` because `exponent < -decimal_pos` is False.\n\nThe issue is that the condition `exponent < -decimal_pos` is checking if the number is smaller than what can be represented with `decimal_pos` decimal places. But this is not the right condition.\n\nActually, I think"
    },
